Key changes made:

1. Removed all JSON.stringify/parse operations
2. Created a single translate function that can be reused
3. Changed the state structure to use direct objects instead of stringified JSON
4. Changed the type property to "object" where appropriate
5. Maintained the function references by not serializing them
6. Directly accessed the value property from state objects instead of parsing them

This should resolve the "t is not a function" error because now the translate function will be properly preserved and passed through to the components. The error was occurring because JSON.stringify cannot serialize functions, so when we parsed the JSON back, the functions were lost.

